# tree
File
  TypeDecl
    LineComment "// Type values, field-type projection, and the storage rule. Every type symbol"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// is, in value position, a compile-time value — immutable, side-effect-free, of"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// the builtin type `type` (the metatype, type : type). Type values are"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// comptime-only: they fold and are gone before any runtime. They can be"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// *consumed* by a comptime expression — an assert, a comparison — but never"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// *stored*: a const, let, field, parameter, or result whose type is `type` is"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// rejected, so a type value cannot escape into a runtime slot. A projected field"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// type is named with a type alias or reused in a type position, never bound to a"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// value."
    Newline "\n"
    Newline "\n"
    DocComment "/// A character level, a nominal alias the schema shares."
    Newline "\n"
